{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.CentralElement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.CentralElement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeH3","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.BorromeanUnique"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.borromean3_not_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.borromean3_not_central","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/CentralElement.lean#L99-L128","doc":"The center of the 3-strand braid group B₃ is infinite cyclic,\ngenerated by the full twist Δ² = (σ₀σ₁σ₀)².\n\nThis is a classical result in braid theory:\n- Chow (1948): Z(B_n) = ⟨Δ²⟩ for n ≥ 3\n- Birman (1974): \"Braids, Links, and Mapping Class Groups\", Thm 1.24\n\nIn our context: Δ² = I in the standard (2,1) representation\n(proved: fullTwist_sq_eq_one), and B₃ = (σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³ ≠ Δ² = I\n(proved: borromean3_ne_fullTwist). Therefore B₃ is NOT in the\ncenter of B₃.\n\nThe confinement uniqueness does NOT require B₃ to be central.\nInstead, B₃ is the unique element with:\n(a) e⁻ = 0 in NF (proved by Hecke engine)\n(b) χ_triv = 1 (proved)\n(c) Confined net matching both proton and neutron targets\n    (proved computationally in confinement-operator-selection.py)\n(d) Minimal braid word length among (a)-(c) satisfying elements ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.borromean3_ne_fullTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.borromean3_ne_fullTwist","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/CentralElement.lean#L77-L89","doc":"B₃ = (σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³ ≠ Δ² = (σ₀σ₁σ₀)² in the standard rep.\nΔ² = I (proved above), but B₃ ≠ I (proved above).\nTherefore B₃ ≠ Δ². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.fullTwist_sq_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.fullTwist_sq_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/CentralElement.lean#L53-L73","doc":"The full twist Δ = σ₀σ₁σ₀ squares to the identity in the\nstandard (2,1) representation of H₃(q).\n\nThis is because Δ² is central with character q^{n(λ)} on\nirrep V_λ, and for λ = (2,1) the content is 0, so Δ² ↦ I.\n\nNumerically verified: (σ₀σ₁σ₀)² = I at all tested q values. ","signatureChunk":0}]}